# Production-only defaults. Committed on purpose: these are PUBLIC values that
# ship in the page source, not secrets. Never put keys/passwords in this file —
# real secrets (PAYPAL_*, RESEND_API_KEY, ADMIN_PASSWORD, CANCEL_TOKEN_SECRET)
# belong in the Vercel dashboard only.
#
# Next.js reads this file only when NODE_ENV=production (`next build`), so
# `npm run dev` never picks it up and local browsing stays out of the analytics
# data. Vercel dashboard env vars take precedence over this file if ever set.

# Google Analytics 4 measurement ID.
# The measurement ID of the "Mokaru Website" stream in the Mokaru GA4 property
# (stream 11184002450). It read G-GX0GTPCYPG from 2026-07-17 until 2026-09-03 —
# an ID that belongs to no property the owner can see, so every hit from this
# site went nowhere for 48 days. The tag was verified to FIRE at the time; that
# it ARRIVED was never checked, and GA4 answers 2xx to an unknown ID.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-47EBNJP8MX
